codex
The fixed semantics exposes an unbounded list structurally through its `for` iterator, while the index-based `while` keeps elements hidden behind symbolic random access and needs an extra universal indexing lemma. I’m switching to an equivalent single-pass `for` implementation with explicit `i` and `previous`; it preserves the contract and examples, and gives the prover one native sequence constructor per circularity—the sound structural-induction shape recommended by the Kit.
apply patch
