The entry claim is not reusing the circularity promptly, so I’m stopping the unbounded run before it wastes memory and comparing its bounded state against the passing loop claim. The most likely mismatch is a single exact frame or continuation term introduced by the function call.
diff --git a/smoke.py b/smoke.py
new file mode 100644
